1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,208
A whole capital city, covered in white
marble.

2
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:07,852
This is Turkmenistan, known as the Land of
White Marble.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,795
Its capital is Ashgabat.

4
00:00:10,650 --> 00:00:15,277
About 7 million people live here, on
488,000 square kilometers.

5
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:18,818
They speak Turkmen. Hello is salam.

6
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:21,754
And they pay with the Turkmen manat.

7
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,604
Here are some facts worth remembering. And
stay until the end,

8
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:29,659
for a mystery nobody ever solved.

9
00:00:31,150 --> 00:00:33,920
Ashgabat holds a Guinness World Record for

10
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:36,996
the highest density of white marble
buildings.

11
00:00:37,546 --> 00:00:40,719
In 2013, the count reached 543.

12
00:00:41,269 --> 00:00:45,046
In 2002, the president renamed the months
of the year.

13
00:00:45,596 --> 00:00:49,074
January became Türkmenbaşy, and April took
his mother's name.

14
00:00:49,624 --> 00:00:51,707
The old names came back in 2008.

15
00:00:52,257 --> 00:00:57,302
From 1993, gas, electricity and water were
free for every household.

16
00:00:57,852 --> 00:01:00,855
That lasted more than 25 years, until
2019.

17
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,940
Grab your bag, we're going exploring.

18
00:01:05,217 --> 00:01:09,412
First, the Darvaza gas crater, nicknamed
the Door to Hell.

19
00:01:09,962 --> 00:01:13,081
It is about 70 meters wide, and it has
burned for decades.

20
00:01:13,631 --> 00:01:16,727
Next, Kow Ata, an underground lake hidden
in a cave.

21
00:01:17,277 --> 00:01:20,487
Its warm water lies more than 50 meters
below the surface.

22
00:01:21,037 --> 00:01:24,113
Then Yangykala Canyon, the Fiery
Fortresses.

23
00:01:24,663 --> 00:01:27,607
Its colorful cliffs once lay under an
ancient sea.

24
00:01:28,157 --> 00:01:30,389
Ancient Merv was a major Silk Road city.

25
00:01:30,939 --> 00:01:33,111
UNESCO listed it in 1999.

26
00:01:33,661 --> 00:01:37,300
And Kunya-Urgench, with a minaret about 60
meters tall.

27
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:39,998
It joined the UNESCO list in 2005.

28
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:42,683
Ten dollars. What can you buy?

29
00:01:44,883 --> 00:01:48,693
At the official rate, your $10 become 35
manat.

30
00:01:49,243 --> 00:01:52,611
A city bus ride in Ashgabat costs half a
manat.

31
00:01:53,161 --> 00:01:55,977
A plate of plov at the bazaar, about 20.

32
00:01:56,527 --> 00:01:59,836
5 liters of gas, at 1.5 manat per liter.

33
00:02:00,386 --> 00:02:05,258
But a loaf of bread costs about 7 manat.
That's more than in the United States.

34
00:02:05,808 --> 00:02:10,479
So with $10, you get a bus ride, a plate
of plov, 5 liters of gas,

35
00:02:10,499 --> 00:02:12,845
and one loaf of bread. That's it.

36
00:02:13,395 --> 00:02:18,349
Unless you change money on the street,
where $10 get you almost 6 times more.

37
00:02:18,369 --> 00:02:19,596
But that's illegal.

38
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:23,211
Before you do anything, here's what not to
do.

39
00:02:24,683 --> 00:02:28,342
Don’t photograph police stations,
airports, or government buildings.

40
00:02:28,892 --> 00:02:31,595
Don’t stay more than 3 working days
without registering.

41
00:02:32,145 --> 00:02:35,145
Don’t smoke outside, except in marked
smoking areas.

42
00:02:35,695 --> 00:02:38,658
Don’t buy a carpet without its export
certificate.

43
00:02:39,208 --> 00:02:42,915
And don’t drive a dirty car in Ashgabat.
The police can fine you.

44
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:46,877
What makes this place unique? Its culture.

45
00:02:48,417 --> 00:02:53,057
The national dish is often said to be
dograma, meat and bread in a rich broth.

46
00:02:53,607 --> 00:02:56,197
The telpek is a tall sheepskin hat.

47
00:02:56,747 --> 00:02:58,617
It is a symbol of Turkmen pride.

48
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:01,967
And the dutar is a two-string lute.

49
00:03:02,517 --> 00:03:05,297
It joined the UNESCO heritage list in
2021.

50
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:08,134
How did this country get here?

51
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:13,980
Back in 1924, the Turkmen Soviet republic
was created.

52
00:03:14,530 --> 00:03:19,047
Then came 1948: a huge earthquake nearly
destroyed Ashgabat.

53
00:03:19,597 --> 00:03:23,789
Fast forward to 1991, when Turkmenistan
declared independence.

54
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:28,303
And finally, what you stayed for: legends
and mysteries.

55
00:03:29,850 --> 00:03:35,020
First, a legend. Gorogly was born in a
grave, after his mother died.

56
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:37,790
His name means son of the grave.

57
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:43,994
He grew up to lead forty horsemen against
cruel rulers, riding his winged horse,

58
00:03:44,014 --> 00:03:44,440
Gyrat.

59
00:03:44,990 --> 00:03:49,650
Bards still sing his story, and UNESCO
listed the epic in 2015.

60
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:55,870
Now, a mystery. In the Karakum desert lie
the ruins of Gonur Depe,

61
00:03:55,890 --> 00:03:58,390
a city about 4,000 years old.

62
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:02,760
It had palaces, temples, and graves full
of treasure.

63
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:06,980
Then its people left, and no one knows
exactly why.

64
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:10,630
One theory says the river that fed the
city moved away.

65
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:15,730
And the last mystery: how did the Door to
Hell really begin?

66
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:20,393
The famous story says Soviet geologists
drilled there in 1971,

67
00:04:20,413 --> 00:04:22,080
and the ground collapsed.

68
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:25,520
They lit the gas, hoping it would burn out
in a few days.

69
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:30,750
But no official record has ever been
found, and the fire still burns.

70
00:04:33,700 --> 00:04:35,089
That was Turkmenistan.

71
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:38,049
Which country should we visit next? Tell
me in the comments.
